# Default deny: only build manifests, Python code, and five curated reports enter the context.
**
!Dockerfile
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
# The Module 4 source digest explicitly hashes this Compose contract.
!compose.yaml
!deploy/dashboard/requirements/api.txt
!deploy/dashboard/requirements/ui.txt
!deploy/dashboard/requirements/ui-dev.txt
!deploy/dashboard/requirements/browser.txt
!src/**/*.py
!tests/**/*.py
tests/test_k8s_*.py
# Every script is Python source and is admitted as a tree. Docker matches a
# directory allow-list against each file beneath it, so a per-file list here
# would be redundant; which scripts actually reach an image is decided by the
# COPY instructions in the Dockerfile, not by this file.
!scripts/

# These exclusions remain last so future allowlist changes cannot include local state or secrets.
**/.git/**
**/results/**
**/data/**
**/checkpoints/**
**/spark-warehouse/**
**/metastore_db/**
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/**
**/.ruff_cache/**
**/.mypy_cache/**
**/.venv/**
**/venv/**
**/node_modules/**
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/secrets/**
**/credentials/**
**/private/**
**/*secret*
**/*credential*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
